        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/ssrf-unauthenticated-egress-ip-disclosure",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "SSRF / unauthenticated egress IP disclosure — No issue identified: GET /api/status.php public_ip field (detect_public_ip)\n\nControl: detect_public_ip() at php/bootstrap.php:117-139 has no user input — curl_init('https://api.ipify.org') is a hardcoded string on line 124. Triggered via GET /api/status.php pre-auth (response captured: HTTP 200, {\"ok\":true,\"connected\":false,\"username\":null,\"sandbox\":false,\"csrf\":\"9c09...\",\"mailcow_origin\":\"https://host.docker.internal\",\"public_ip\":\"146.70.126.61\"}). The response leaks: server egress IP, session CSRF token (session-bound, not a static secret), mailcow_origin built from HTTP_HOST (reflects the request, not new info). Cache file CRED_DIR/.publicip written with default perms (no chmod, unlike store_credentials which chmods to 0600) — inside CRED_DIR which store_credentials chmods to 0700; not an additional exposure beyond the pre-auth status.php disclosure itself. Assessed as info disclosure only."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "GET /api/status.php public_ip field (detect_public_ip)"
                }
