        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/bfla-authentication-bypass-method-level-authorization",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "BFLA / authentication bypass / method-level authorization — No issue identified: POST /api/mcp.php (php/mcp.php)\n\nAuth gate confirmed at php/mcp.php:107-114 (getenv('MAILCOW_API_KEY') → Bearer regex → hash_equals → json_err 401), executed before ALL method dispatch (initialize:129, notifications/:137, tools/call:144). Dynamic: POST initialize no auth → 401, wrong Bearer → 401, GET wrong Bearer → 401 (order: auth before POST check — wrong-key GET leaks only the 401 body, never the 405 method hint), tools/call no auth → 401, notifications/initialized no auth → 401. Proxy ids 18,19,20,28,29,91,92,33. hash_equals timing-safe; Bearer regex (multi-token 'Bearer x y' fails match → 401); empty/unset key short-circuits to 401 (verified live PHP 8.4 harness, fail-closed). Correct-key control passes gate (reaches 400 Invalid JSON-RPC), proving the gate is the only barrier. No BFLA/bypass found."
          },
          "locations": [
