          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/xxe-entity-expansion-dtd-transclusion-on-upstream-xml",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "XXE / entity expansion / DTD transclusion on upstream XML — Ruled out: php/namecheap.php nc_call simplexml_load_string (upstream XML parse)\n\nControl: PHP's libxml2 >= 2.9 disables external entity loading by default. nc_call() at php/namecheap.php:39 parses with @simplexml_load_string($body) — no LIBXML_NOENT flag passed (the only flags bit used is default 0), so external entity resolution is off. Verified this runtime build: PHP 8.4.24 CLI in the sandbox with libxml 2.15.3 (LIBXML_VERSION=21503), simplexml external-entity file read against a real local canary returned empty content by default; adding LIBXML_NOENT fetched the canary content — proving the flag is what enables it and it is absent in namecheap.php. Dynamic local snippet: php /tmp/xxe_probe.php + /tmp/xxe_probe3.php. The XML body comes from an operator-configured endpoint (nc-mock:8088 in this deployment), not directly from attacker input; no DTD/parameter-entity transclusion path is enabled."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "php/namecheap.php nc_call simplexml_load_string (upstream XML parse)"
                }
