          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/mass-assignment-unrestricted-attrs-passthrough-to-mailcow-edit-domain",
          "ruleIndex": 8,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Mass assignment / unrestricted attrs passthrough to mailcow edit/domain — Ruled out: mcp_tool_call set_domain_settings (php/mcp.php:97-102)\n\nphp/mcp.php:97-102 forwards the caller's attrs object 1:1 as {'items':[$domain],'attr':$attrs} to mailcow POST /api/v1/edit/domain — no key allowlist (verified: no array_intersect_key in file). Dangerous keys ARE forwardable (active:\"0\", backupmx/relay_all_recipients:\"1\", maxquota/defquota overrides, rl_value/rl_frame per the tool description at line 69) — verified by encoding a hostile attrs payload. However the only caller must hold the read-write MAILCOW_API_KEY (php/mcp.php:112 gate), which could call mailcow's own admin API directly with identical effect — no privilege added, and the tool contract documents read/write domain management. Cannot dynamically confirm (no real key); assessed source-only within the trust boundary. Not a vulnerability by itself."
          },
