          "message": {
            "text": "Spoofed ClientIp / authz-trust on client-supplied IP — No issue identified: POST /api/connect.php client_ip param\n\nconnect.php:13 reads user-supplied client_ip, validates with FILTER_VALIDATE_IP (400 on invalid), passes to nc_call as ClientIp param. detect_public_ip() only runs when client_ip is empty (connect.php:33-34). Server-side consequence: none — client_ip is never read back for any authz or trust decision; rg over php/ shows its only readers are nc_call param building (namecheap.php:12) and the IP-not-whitelisted error message construction (namecheap.php:44-46). Namecheap gates by the real source IP of the server, not this parameter. Attacker can claim any IP in the outbound call; assessed honestly as low/info."
