          "message": {
            "text": "Object-level authz / domain parameter injection (SSRF-like smuggle to upstream API) — No issue identified: GET /api/dns.php?domain= (php/dns.php)\n\nphp/dns.php:158 gates on require_namecheap_session() before any domain handling. Dynamic: no cookie → 401 (proxy ids 85/86, 9). Domain regex (php/dns.php:161, same pattern as mcp.php:86) validated with PHP 8.4 against 26 payloads — ALL rejected except benign: query smuggle (example.com?x=1), '-a- evil.com', '../etc/passwd', encoded traversal, null bytes, fragments, slashes, unicode raw, punycode-no-TLD, 64-char labels, 313-char names, cloud metadata IP, [::1], empty/leading labels, uppercase, trailing dot — all rejected. Legit punycode (xn--80ak6aa92e.com) and 63-char labels accepted; 4-label 253-char name ACCEPTED, 255 rejected (length boundary enforced). DomainName reaches Namecheap only post-regex (php/dns.php:165 → php/namecheap.php:85 passes ['DomainName' => $domain]). No injection/smuggle vector."
