          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/csrf-require-csrf-gate-placement-vs-rate-limit-token-single-use-session-bound-timing-safe",
          "ruleIndex": 14,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "CSRF (require_csrf gate placement vs rate limit; token single-use / session-bound / timing-safe) — No issue identified: POST /api/connect.php\n\nCSRF gate confirmed on this endpoint: POST /api/connect.php without any token -> 403 'Invalid CSRF token, reload the page'; require_csrf() runs BEFORE register_failed_attempt() per source (php/connect.php:9), so the gate is not affected by and does not burn the per-session rate limit. Same control set as disconnect.php (hash_equals + session-bound token + SameSite=Lax); forgery not demonstrated. Token non-rotating and pre-auth fetchable per-session (status.php) — residual risks noted in findings note 7fa3e2; session fixation is the compounding weakness (Session-Validator's scope)."
