          "message": {
            "text": "CSRF token issuance & session binding — No issue identified: GET /api/status.php\n\nGET /api/status.php returns the session csrf to any unauthenticated visitor: 32 hex chars (16 random bytes via bin2hex(random_bytes(16)), php/bootstrap.php:36-42), stored in $_SESSION — same cookie returns the same token (persistent, non-rotating), different cookie returns a different token. Set-Cookie: MULTIAI_LANDING=...; path=/; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax (no Secure flag over plain HTTP). Pre-auth fetchability is session-scoped and harmless alone; compounding risk only with session fixation (documented in findings note 7fa3e2)."
